# 🔴 APPLIES TO THE PIN THAT IS LIVE RIGHT NOW, not only to future ones.
three_step_upgrade: >-
  Taking a657f4f is install -> `uis dagster run klass_refresh` -> `uis dagster run
  transform_and_publish`. The middle step is NOT optional: transform_and_publish rebuilds
  mart_dim_kommune from raw.ssb_klass_kommuner but never re-fetches it, so deploy-then-transform
  rebuilds the same stale rows and 3e72760 (Klass window widened 1960 -> 1950) is inert with
  every signal green. Anything pinned after a657f4f inherits the requirement unless atlas says
  the refresh has already run everywhere.
  CORRECTION to what this file said before (#1373): the claim "the artifact does not say this"
  was WRONG. The pinned artifact names klass_refresh twice — first_data.jobs lists it SECOND,
  before transform_and_publish, and the monthly cadence row names it — so a FIRST INSTALL
  following first_data.jobs already gets the right order. This repo's own verifier prints that
  job list on every run. The real gap was that the artifact had no concept of an UPGRADE, and
  operational.upgrade (merged upstream at 6cb28f4) closes it by stating the RULE rather than
  another job list. a657f4f does NOT carry operational.upgrade, so the page still hand-carries
  the sequence; that stops when a build with the field is pinned.
  🔴 AND IT SELF-HEALS, which is why the ordering mistake stayed invisible: klass_refresh runs
  `0 1 1 * *`, so an unrun re-ingest repairs itself at 01:00 on the 1st — up to a month later,
  with no record of why the failure cleared.

